  "scope": "Prospective study of actual bounded native-history reading in three-round research on a new partition of familiar Servo and a disclosed label-permuted control. Two paired cases, four complete projects. Same516 genuinely evaluated seed candidates, baseline fact, unscored family batch catalog, instructions, model, query actions, budget and confirmation. A uses current full native records; B omits repeated artifact_records and input_artifact_bindings only after full qualification/record limits. All observation values/validation/scopes/evaluator identities remain intact, plus complete-record digest. No runtime default change. Measure actual late evidence consumption and its use, new/duplicate programs, final quality and full costs. Initial history is a predeclared CPU search, not fabricated scores or a model-generated long campaign. No memory isolation, independent population, or broad stable capability claim."
